  {
   "id": 509669,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"4 \\times {10^7} + 0 \\times {10^6} + 6 \\times {10^5} + 3 \\times {10^4} + 0 \\times {10^3} + 8 \\times {10^2} + 9 \\times {10^1} + 1 \\times {10^0}\">4 \\times {10^7} + 0 \\times {10^6} + 6 \\times {10^5} + 3 \\times {10^4} + 0 \\times {10^3} + 8 \\times {10^2} + 9 \\times {10^1} + 1 \\times {10^0}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"4 \\times {10^7} + 0 \\times {10^6} + 6 \\times {10^5} + 3 \\times {10^4} + 0 \\times {10^3} + 8 \\times {10^2} + 9 \\times {10^1} + 1 \\times {10^0}\"></span></p>\n<p>Remember that any base raised to the exponent 0 is 1.</p>\n<p>Use the order of expressions (PEMDAS), which means</p>\n<p>do the exponents first,</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4 \\times 10,000,000 + 0 \\times 1,000,000 + 6 \\times 100,000 + 3 \\times 10,000 + 0 \\times 1,000 + 8 \\times 100 + 9 \\times 10 + 1 \\times 1\"></span></p>\n<p>then multiplications,</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"40,000,000 + 0 + 600,000 + 30,000 + 0 + 800 + 90 + 1\"></span></p>\n<p>then additions.</p>\n<p>40,630,891</p>"
    },
